id_carrier.py; rg -n -A 8 '\"'^'\"\\\\[design\\\\.LLR-337\\\\]' docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml\"","aggregated_output":"# WI-978 spine change list (stage 1, the tests)\n\nNo registry was edited. Proposed changes, for the coordinator and the P15 reconciliation:\n\n1. TC-402 `evidence` (Drafted): add the landing-table cases the row's method drives (\"Drive every\n   landing-table outcome ... on both callers\") but its evidence cell does not name:\n   - `tests/test_id_landing.py::test_the_slot_refuses_each_unreserved_landing` (5 params: no-record,\n     another-wis-record, retired-number, no-carrier, landing-only-record)\n   - `tests/test_id_landing.py::test_the_slot_rung_refuses_ids_added_under_an_unreadable_claim`\n   - `tests/test_id_landing.py::test_the_slot_lands_a_lane_whose_ids_sit_in_its_own_record`\n     (characterization, row 2 at the slot)\n   - `tests/test_id_landing.py::test_a_code_only_lane_with_no_carrier_lands` (characterization,\n     row 1 at the slot)\n   - `tests/test_id_landing.py::test_a_watermark_conflict_beside_another_conflict_still_refuses`\n     (characterization, the plan's P7 refresh guard)\n   - `tests/test_id_landing.py::test_the_hand_squash_refuses_each_unreserved_landing` (5 params)\n   - `tests/test_id_landing.py::test_the_hand_squash_passes_ids_in_its_own_record`\n   - `tests/test_id_landing.py::test_the_hand_squash_refuses_ids_added_under_an_unreadable_claim`\n2. TC-158 `evidence` (Approved; amended in this lane's intent set): two tests not in the cell,\n   proposed for addition at the checkpoint (or left out, the coordinator's call):\n   - `tests/test_id_watermark.py::test_an_unchanged_committed_baseline_passes_the_floor` (the\n     control for the git-baseline cases)\n   - `tests/test_id_watermark.py::test_the_live_id_finding_points_a_lane_at_the_reserve_verb` (the\n     plan's P4 text change: the live-id finding names `--reserve-ids`)\n3. LLR-363 `code_symbol` (binds at P15): the tests fix two trace seams the cell does not list,\n   `live_ids` and `live_ids_at` (the one live-id sweep, over the working tree and over a git tree).\n4. LLR-362 `code_symbol` (binds at P15): the tests use `Refused` (the one refusal type of the\n   argument parsers); the plan's P4 also names `record_history_findings`, which no test calls\n   directly (it is driven through the CLI).\n\nNo test is named differently from a name a row already gives: every evidence entry in TC-158,\nTC-401 and TC-402 exists under that exact name.\n\n\n# Stage 2 (P2 to P5, the carrier code) additions\n\nNo registry was edited. Names the code built that the intent rows do not give (for the P15\nreconciliation; each binds there):\n\n5. LLR-362 `code_symbol`: the built names beyond the cell's list.\n   - In `project-trajectory/scripts/id_carrier.py`: `WATERMARK`, `MAX_COUNT`, `LOST_RACE`,\n     `RESERVE_VERB`, `CORRECTION_LINE`, `Refused` (an alias of `ValueError`, see 7),\n     `parse_marks`, `parse_corrections` (moved from trace.py, see 6), `record_line`, `reserve`\n     (the reservation's orchestration: argument checks, the trunk claim, the plan, the carrier\n     write), `receiving_sides` (the receiving file's sides, stages 2 and 3 when conflicted),\n     `record_history_findings` (the committed-record union check). Private helpers: `_count`,\n     `_ref_value`, `_plumb`, `_claimed`, `_id_name`, `_outside_lines`.\n   - In `project-trajectory/scripts/trace.py`: `reserve_ids` (the `--reserve-ids` verb's library\n     call; IF-101's `data` already names it), `committed_reservations`, `_baseline_texts` (the one\n     parent walk the three committed readers share), `_reserved_highs`, `_basis`,\n     `_render_full`, `_trunk_name`, `_committed_marks` (was `_watermark_at`, now over a text the shared walk\n     reads), `_cmd_reserve_ids`, `_cmd_fold_ids`; `watermark_findings` gains a\n     `previous_reservations` argument. `parse_corrections` stays a trace name (an alias of the\n     moved reader).\n6. LLR-362 `module`/`code_symbol`: `parse_corrections` (and the correction-line grammar) moved\n   from trace.py into id_carrier.py, because the fold unions correction records over texts and\n   must read them with the one grammar; trace.py keeps `parse_corrections` as an alias, so no\n   caller changed. Not the S5 \"move the watermark section\" refactor: only the line grammars the\n   fold reads moved.\n7. LLR-362: `Refused` is `ValueError` itself, not a subclass. `tests/test_id_carrier.py` loads the\n   module afresh for every symbol it reads (`_ic()` per `_sym` call), so a class defined in the\n   module is a different class per load and `pytest.raises(<load A's Refused>)` misses load B's\n   raise. Proposed: either keep the alias (as built) or change the test to load the module once,\n   then restore a dedicated subclass.\n8. IF-101 `data` names the fold verb as `fold_ids`; the built library call is `fold_watermark`\n   (the name LLR-363's `code_symbol` already gives) and the CLI flag is `--fold-ids`. Proposed:\n   IF-101 `data` reads `fold_watermark` (or keeps `fold_ids` as the verb's name; the coordinator's\n   call).\n9. `project-trajectory/scripts/kitlib/git.py` `git_bytes` gains an optional `stdin` (bytes, fed\n   untranslated): the carrier's `hash-object --stdin` and `mktree` input must not have its\n   newlines turned into CRLF on Windows, which `git_out`'s text-mode `stdin` does. Its owning\n   rows (the kitlib git seam) are outside this spec's named surface; no row cell names the\n   argument list, so no cell change is proposed, only noted.\n10. IF-224 `data` (Drafted; owner `scripts/agent_common`, requestor `scripts/trace`): the\n    reservation reads the declared trunk's name through `agent_common.trunk_name`, from\n    `trace._trunk_name` (a deferred import, the same edge IF-224 declares), so the claim check\n    asks the kit's one trunk reader. IF-224's `data` names only `human_approves_spine`.\n    Proposed: IF-224 `data` gains \"trunk_name(root) -> the declared trunk's name, or raises\n    TrunkUndeclared\" (or IF-179, which already states `trunk_name`, gains `scripts/trace` as a\n    requestor; the coordinator's call). The first build placed the read in `id_carrier`, which\n    made a new CMP-006 -> CMP-008 edge with no seam (`check_trajectory --strict` ERROR) and a new\n    deferred import edge (`tests/test_import_layers.py`'s stamped window); moving it to trace\n    reuses the declared edge and leaves both green.\n\n\n# Stage 3 (P6 to P9, the landing) additions\n\nNo registry was edited. Names the code built that the intent rows do not give (for the P15\nreconciliation; each binds there):\n\n11. LLR-363 `code_symbol`: the built names beyond the cell's list. In\n    `project-trajectory/scripts/trace.py`: `live_ids` (the one live-id sweep, `live_max_ids` now\n    derives from it), `live_ids_at` (the sweep at a git tree). In\n    `project-trajectory/scripts/integrate.py`: `_fold_watermark_conflict` (a refresh conflict on\n    the watermark settled by the fold), `_fold_carrier_in` (the refresh's carrier fold after\n    merging trunk in), `WATERMARK`; `_merge_refusal` gains the rung (already a symbol of other\n    rows), `integrate_one` calls `_landing_ready`. In `project-trajectory/scripts/check.py`:\n    `_reserved_ids_refusal` (the step's judgement), `_squash_work_items` (the squashed lane's\n    claim read), `FOLD_REMEDY`; `_reserved_ids_mode` is in the cell already.\n12. LLR-363 `module`: the shipped `project-trajectory/hooks/pre-commit` now runs the\n    `reserved-ids` step in its batched floor (the plan's P8); proposed: the module cell gains the\n    hook, as LLR-358 carries it for its own step.\n13. LLR-362 `code_symbol`: in `project-trajectory/scripts/id_carrier.py`, the landing's git half\n    that keeps trace.py's growth down: `LANDING_DIRS`, `ids_at` (a sweep over a tree-ish's two\n    registry directories, written out), `_added_ids`, `landing_refusal` (the six-row judgement\n    over git: added ids, carrier records, landing and parent records; a tree the sweep cannot\n    read refuses), `rev_fold_lag` (the fold lag of a tree-ish's watermark), `_watermark_at`.\n    `Refused` is a `ValueError` subclass again (item 7 settled: the test helper loads the module\n    once).\n14. LLR-181 (Approved; `kitlib/git.py` is in its module cell) `code_symbol`: the plan's lift of\n    re-judge's archive extractor into `kitlib.git` added `extract_paths` and `ArchiveError`\n    (tagged `Implements: SR-166, LLR-181`); rejudge's `_archive_chunk` now calls it and keeps its\n    own `RejudgeError` (its tests unchanged). Proposed: append both names to LLR-181's cell at\n    the next sitting that touches it, or name a different home; no cell was edited.\n15. LLR-337 (Approved; `kitlib/git.py` is in its module cell) `code_symbol`: the plan's lift of\n    the lanes-containing-tip read added `lanes_containing` (tagged `Implements: SR-154,\n    LLR-337`); `plan_gate._squash_lines` is its first caller, `check._squash_work_items` its\n    second. Proposed: append it to LLR-337's cell; no cell was edited.\n16. TC-402 `evidence` (Drafted): add\n    `tests/test_id_landing.py::test_the_pre_commit_hook_runs_the_reserved_ids_step` (the hook\n    wiring pin the plan's P8 asks for).\n17. Two existing tests needed a fixture line, not an assertion change, because the new rung sits\n    right after R1 (the plan's P7) and their lanes add a registry id with no reservation: each now\n    plants a carrier record for the id it adds, so the rung passes the lane on to the rung the\n    test measures.\n    - `tests/test_integrate_admission.py::test_a_lane_that_mints_a_row_born_approved_is_refused`\n      (SR 2-2 for WI-401); its TC's evidence cell is unchanged.\n    - `tests/test_held_status_git.py::test_an_off_spine_demotion_and_a_born_Drafted_row_land_from_a_loop_lane`\n      (B 3-3 for WI-401).\n\n\n# Stage 4 (P10 to P13, the text) additions\n\nNo registry was edited.\n\n18. The landing judgement checks its sixth table row (a landing watermark record that neither\n    the carrier nor the parent holds) only when the landing adds carrier-space ids:\n    `id_carrier.landing_lines` returns at once when nothing is added. The spec's table lists the\n    row on its own; the built code reads row 1 (\"no carrier-space id added: passes\") first. The\n    stage-4 texts (trace.py's IF-101 header, runtime flow 9, the RESYNC entry) state the built\n    behaviour. If LLR-363's or TC-402's wording reads the row as unconditional, it either gains\n    \"when ids are added\" at the reconcile, or the code changes in a later stage (not done here:\n    this stage changes no behaviour).\n19. TC-402 or a coordinator-text TC (none exists; the coordinator tooling is outside the\n    component map): the new pins in `tests/test_prompts.py`,\n    `test_the_terra_brief_drafts_new_ids_only_from_its_reserved_ranges` and\n    `test_the_cycle_reserves_before_drafting_and_folds_the_watermark` (3 params), verify the\n    procedure text only. No row is proposed to cite them; noted for the coordinator.\n\n\n# Fix round 1 (the 6701eec reviews) additions\n\nNo registry was edited.\n\n20. TC-402 `evidence` (Drafted): add three regression tests in `tests/test_id_landing.py`:\n    - `test_a_registry_an_export_ignore_rule_hides_is_still_judged` (the judgement at a lane tip\n      and the hand squash's `reserved-ids` step, with a committed `export-ignore` rule over the\n      registries);\n    - `test_the_slot_refuses_an_unreserved_id_an_export_ignore_rule_hides` (the merge slot, same\n      rule);\n    - `test_a_registry_conflict_beside_the_watermark_refuses_with_the_merge_undone` (a refresh\n      whose registry conflicts beside the watermark refuses, branch tip unmoved, lane clean).\n21. TC-401 `evidence` (Drafted): add\n    `tests/test_id_carrier_git.py::test_a_reservation_in_a_lane_behind_trunk_commits_through_the_integrity_floor`\n    and `tests/test_id_carrier.py::test_the_carrier_contributes_only_its_records_and_the_marks_they_justify`.\n    `tests/test_id_carrier.py::test_a_carrier_mark_above_the_files_is_a_lag` is renamed\n    `test_a_recorded_mark_above_the_files_is_a_lag` (no evidence cell named the old name).\n22. LLR-362 `code_symbol` (binds at P15): `carried` (the carrier's contribution to a working\n    file's fold: its records and the marks they justify) and `MARK_LINE` (the one mark-line\n    grammar, now public; trace's strict readers and `retire.read_marks` read it).\n23. LLR-181 `code_symbol` (Approved; `kitlib/git.py` in its module cell): `write_blobs` and\n    `_listed_blobs` (tagged `Implements: SR-166, LLR-181`, beside `extract_paths`): the landing's\n    tree read now writes each registry blob by object id, so no attribute drops or rewrites one;\n    `extract_paths` keeps one caller, `rejudge`. Proposed with item 14 at the next sitting that\n    touches LLR-181, or a different home named.\n24. A semantic reading for the checkpoint (LLR-362/LLR-363 text unchanged; TC-401's method may\n    want it): the fold's carrier side contributes the carrier's reservation records and, per\n    space, the highest number they reserve, never the carrier's other mark lines (those hold\n    trunk's marks as of each reservation and are the allocation floor only). The spec's S3\n    \"for each space, the maximum mark\" is read as the maximum over the receiving sides and that\n    contribution. At a landing or refresh trunk is a parent, so the landed result is unchanged;\n    in a lane cut before a trunk mint it is what makes the folded file committable. The fold\n    lag reads the same contribution.\n25. LLR-363: the refresh folds a watermark conflict only when it is the sole conflicted path\n    (its detail already says \"a refresh conflict limited to the watermark resolves to that fold;\n    any other conflict remains refused\"; no cell change proposed).\n26. `retire.py` now imports `id_carrier` (an intra-CMP-006 edge; `retire.read_marks` reads through\n    `id_carrier.parse_marks`). LLR-286's `code_symbol` does not list `read_marks`; no cell\n    change proposed.\n\n\n# Fix round 2 (the e5ecf9d reviews) additions\n\nNo registry was edited.\n\n27. TC-402 `evidence` (Drafted): add the slot regression test\n    `tests/test_id_landing.py::test_the_slot_lands_a_code_only_lane_after_trunk_deletes_an_id_it_based_on`\n    (a code-only lane whose base holds an id trunk then deletes lands through the merge slot,\n    unrefreshed; it failed on the pre-fix rung, which compared the tip with trunk's tip).\n    TC-402's `method` may want \"and a code-only lane after trunk retired an id from its base\"\n    beside \"a stale-base lane that minted another lane's reserved number\".\n28. LLR-363 `detail` (Drafted), for the checkpoint's reading: \"added\" at the automated landing is\n    over the lane's base (its merge base with trunk, the delta the mint rung reads); at the hand\n    landing it is over HEAD (git's squash is already merged onto it). The cell says neither \"parent\"\n    nor \"base\", so no change is required; if the sitting wants the reading stated, \"an identity\n    the landing adds over the tree its change is made on\" covers both routes. LLR-363\n    `code_symbol` gains `_lane_base` (integrate.py; the R1 mint rung shares it).\n29. LLR-362 `code_symbol`: `check_work_item` is unchanged as a name but now lives in trace.py\n    (already in the row's module cell): it reads the reserve verb's argument through the kit's one\n    lane-input parser, `agent_common.parse_wi_id`. `id_carrier.reserve` takes the checked id;\n    `id_carrier._claimed` is deleted.\n30. IF-224 `data` (Drafted; extends item 10): the tracer's deferred `agent_common` import now also\n    reads `parse_wi_id(value, source) -> the one WI id, or raises ValueError` for the reserve\n    verb's work-item check (IF-179 gaining `scripts/trace`, if that row already states the parser,\n    is the alternative; the coordinator's call).\n31. LLR-141 (Approved; `kitlib/git.py` in its module cell, `claimed_w