ration branch, and at a hand landing also one\n    the staged tree adds over the integration branch's tip\".\n35. TC-402 `expected` / `method` (Drafted): add the case \"a reserved identity authored, retired\n    through the retirement command and authored again inside the same reservation is refused at\n    both landings, naming the identity and its record\"; and \"a stale-base lane whose drafted number\n    another lane landed first is refused at the hand landing too\". `evidence` gains\n    `tests/test_id_landing.py::test_the_slot_refuses_a_retired_id_re_authored_inside_its_own_reservation`,\n    `tests/test_id_landing.py::test_the_hand_squash_refuses_a_retired_id_re_authored_inside_its_own_reservation`,\n    `tests/test_id_landing.py::test_the_hand_squash_refuses_another_lanes_number_after_that_lane_landed`,\n    `tests/test_id_landing.py::test_the_dispatchers_drain_refreshes_a_lane_whose_watermark_lags_the_carrier`,\n    and (006-REVIEW-B F4) `test_the_slot_refuses_each_unreserved_landing`,\n    `test_the_hand_squash_refuses_each_unreserved_landing`,\n    `test_the_slot_rung_refuses_ids_added_under_an_unreadable_claim`,\n    `test_the_hand_squash_refuses_ids_added_under_an_unreadable_claim`,\n    `test_the_slot_lands_a_lane_whose_ids_sit_in_its_own_record`,\n    `test_the_hand_squash_passes_ids_in_its_own_record` (all in `tests/test_id_landing.py`).\n36. IF-101 `data` (Drafted; with 005-REVIEW-A F2's shortening to a pointer under 160 characters and\n    `fold_watermark` for `fold_ids`): the owner contract in trace.py now states that\n    `landing_id_refusal(root, landing_rev, parent_rev, wi_ids, claim_source, lane=None)` also reads\n    the lane tip's delta over its merge base and the retirement records. A short Data proposal:\n    \"read_watermark, bump_watermark, reserve_ids, fold_watermark, landing_id_refusal, landing_fold_lag\n    over docs/id-watermark and the id carrier ref\" (contract detail stays in trace.py).\n37. IF-257 `data` (Drafted): the retirement