nts: SR-174, LLR-362\n484-    \"\"\"\n--\n510-    \"\"\"The watermark text the tree-ish `rev` holds, or \"\" when it holds none.\n511-\n512:    Implements: SR-174, LLR-362\n513-    \"\"\"\n--\n522-    `kitlib.git.ArchiveError` when git cannot write them.\n523-\n524:    Implements: SR-174, LLR-362\n525-    \"\"\"\n--\n533-    `parent_rev`; none when git reports no change under `LANDING_DIRS`.\n534-\n535:    Implements: SR-174, LLR-362\n536-    \"\"\"\n--\n551-    Raises `kitlib.git.ArchiveError` when the merge base cannot be read.\n552-\n553:    Implements: SR-174, LLR-362\n554-    \"\"\"\n--\n584-    naming why.\n585-\n586:    Implements: SR-174, LLR-362\n587-    \"\"\"\n--\n615-    index's tree) behind the carrier tip; [] with no carrier.\n616-\n617:    Implements: SR-174, LLR-362\n618-    \"\"\"\n3383:[design.LLR-337]\n3384-sr_refs = [\"SR-154\"]\n3385-title = \"Single-plan pass gate\"\n3386-module = \"project-trajectory/scripts/plan_gate.py;project-trajectory/scripts/kitlib/plan_pass.py;project-trajectory/scripts/kitlib/git.py\"\n3387-code_symbol = \"_own_changes/_close_homes/_regenerated/_is_home/build_paths/binding_problem/_unbound/record_problems/_reviewed_problems/_critique_problems/blocking_ids/_cap_problems/_dismissals/_record_lines/commit_lines/_parents/lane_rider/landing_refusal/_squash_lines/_claim_base/staged_lines/main/plan_dir/plan_path/record_path/critique_path/critique_round/bytes_digest/delta/parse/render/blob/plan_digest/done_when_digest/planmode/gate_rows/_unattributed_squash/lane_commit_walk/staged_heads\"\n3388-detail = \"The gate reads only rows claimed by the lane's own active folder at the claim base. The closed planmode set is absent, empty, none, single and dual: absent, empty, none and dual are not gated; single is gated; every other normalized value, and a value that is not a string, is held by name. The closed pre-record change set is the record homes and a close: plan records, review records, decision records, session logs, log fragments, the claimed row's own specification, that specification's move to a closed folder with its report and byte-exact inbound-link redirects, or, as a merge's own changes, the compiled change log and the views the trunk regeneration list names; every other own change is build output. Build output is refused unless a parent holds a pass record binding the row, plan digest and Done-when digest left by the change. A changed pass record is accepted only against its first parent when its nine-key grammar is complete, its delta is none or within and is the plan's own line, its digests match the parent's plan and Done-when, its cited critique is byte-identical in that parent, bound to its reviewed commit and accepted by the verdict grammar, and its dispute pair is both present or both empty; a cited critique record is only round one or round two, and any other round is no record. A second-round non-approval additionally requires an accepted dispute dismissal of every blocking and major finding. At filing and commit creation, the reviewed tree also holds the bound plan bytes and Done-when digest. The gate judges the staged lane change, squash-carried lane commits, and landing lane commits oldest first; a squashed tip that no local branch contains is held by name while the landing tree carries any single or out-of-set claim copy; it compares a merge with every parent and holds unreadable claim copies, diffs, listings, records or parents. Trunk and a lane with no single row are not gated. The Done-when digest a record binds is unmoved by a tick or evidence on a Done-when item, so neither unbinds the record. With the trunk undeclared, a branch whose HEAD holds no claim folder is judged at HEAD; any other branch is refused naming the declaration.\"\n3389-rationale = \"A single-plan item needs one durable, fail-closed release boundary so a skipped hook, rebase, merge or landing cannot turn an unreviewed plan into build output.\"\n3390-test_refs = \"TC-367\"\n3391-status = \"Approved\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command '$_edit = @'\"'\n\"'$ErrorActionPreference='\"'Stop'\n\"'$utf8=[Text.UTF8Encoding]::new($false)\nfunction Edit($path,$section,$key,$value){$t=[IO.File]::ReadAllText($path,[Text.Encoding]::UTF8);if($t.Contains(\"`r\")){throw \"non-LF $path\"};$m=[regex]::Match($t,'\"'(?ms)(\"'^'\"\\\\['+[regex]::Escape(\"'$section)+'\"'\\\\]\\\\n)(.*?)(?=\"'^'\"\\\\[|\\\\z)');if(\"'!$m.Success){throw \"missing $section\"};$b=$m.Groups[2].Value;$p='\"'(?m)\"'^'\"'+[regex]::Escape(\"'$key)+'\"'\\\\s*=.*\"'$'\"';if([regex]::Matches(\"'$b,$p).Count-ne 1){throw \"not one $section $key\"};$nb=[regex]::Replace($b,$p,$value,1);$out=$t.Substring(0,$m.Groups[2].Index)+$nb+$t.Substring($m.Groups[2].Index+$m.Groups[2].Length);if($out.Contains(\"`r\")){throw '\"'CR result'};[IO.File]::WriteAllText(\"'$path,$out,$utf8)}\nEdit '\"'docs/requirements/system-requirements.toml' 'requirement.SR-174' 'title' 'title = \\\"Identity is allocated once and never re-issued\\\"'\nEdit 'docs/requirements/system-requirements.toml' 'requirement.SR-174' 'rationale' 'rationale = \\\"\\\"\\\"Identity allocation is its own decision, not a consequence of serialization: serializing the writer makes a COLLISION unlikely and does nothing about RE-USE, which is the half that silently re-points every commit message and archived document citing the freed id. The non-reuse clause has a \"'`shall` of its own here rather than living in SR-170'\"''s acceptance, which is a cell that cannot mint a requirement. Contributes to SN-025 (the ready frontier ordered deterministically, so two readers of the same registry dispatch the same work) by supplying a work-item identity that names one record for every reader, before and after a deletion. It contributes to SN-027 by assigning the registry identities independently authored by parallel lanes from one reservation record, so concurrent lanes cannot receive the same identity. The keep-or-mint review checks LLR-153, LLR-154, TC-147, TC-148, TC-158, and the SR-170 and SR-173 rationales: each concerns the unchanged work-item allocation half.\\\"\\\"\\\"'\nEdit 'docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml' 'design.LLR-337' 'code_symbol' 'code_symbol = \\\"_own_changes/_close_homes/_regenerated/_is_home/build_paths/binding_problem/_unbound/record_problems/_reviewed_problems/_critique_problems/blocking_ids/_cap_problems/_dismissals/_record_lines/commit_lines/_parents/lane_rider/landing_refusal/_squash_lines/_claim_base/staged_lines/main/plan_dir/plan_path/record_path/critique_path/critique_round/bytes_digest/delta/parse/render/blob/plan_digest/done_when_digest/planmode/gate_rows/_unattributed_squash/lane_commit_walk/staged_heads/lanes_containing\\\"'\nEdit 'docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml' 'design.LLR-363' 'module' 'module = \\\"project-trajectory/scripts/id_carrier.py;project-trajectory/scripts/trace.py;project-trajectory/scripts/integrate.py;project-trajectory/scripts/check.py;project-trajectory/hooks/pre-commit\\\"'\nEdit 'docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml' 'design.LLR-362' 'code_symbol' 'code_symbol = \\\"WATERMARK/MAX_COUNT/LOST_RACE/RESERVE_VERB/CORRECTION_LINE/MARK_LINE/Refused/carrier_spaces/parse_marks/parse_corrections/parse_reservations/record_line/parse_counts/plan_reservation/fold/carried/fold_lag/carrier_tip/carrier_text/write_carrier/reserve/receiving_sides/record_history_findings/reserve_ids/check_work_item/committed_reservations/_baseline_texts/_reserved_highs/_basis/_trunk_name/_committed_marks/_cmd_reserve_ids/_cmd_fold_ids\\\"'\nEdit 'docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml' 'design.LLR-363' 'code_symbol' 'code_symbol = \\\"LANDING_DIRS/ids_at/_added_ids/_read_landing/_outside_lines/_retired_lines/landing_lines/landing_refusal/rev_fold_lag/_watermark_at/live_ids/live_ids_at/landing_id_refusal/landing_fold_lag/fold_watermark/_reserved_id_refusal/_landing_ready/_merge_trunk_in/_lane_base/_fold_watermark_conflict/_fold_carrier_in/_reserved_ids_refusal/_squash_work_items/_reserved_ids_mode/FOLD_REMEDY\\\"'\nEdit 'docs/test/test-cases.toml' 'test.TC-401' 'evidence' 'evidence = \\\"\\\"\\\"tests/test_id_carrier.py; tests/test_id_carrier_git.py::test_first_reservation_seeds_the_carrier_from_trunk; tests/test_id_carrier_git.py::test_a_lost_race_refuses_with_nothing_written; tests/test_id_carrier_git.py::test_sequential_reservations_are_disjoint; tests/test_id_carrier_git.py::test_stale_base_reservations_are_disjoint; tests/test_id_carrier_git.py::test_a_reservation_after_a_ruled_correction_starts_above_it; tests/test_id_carrier_git.py::test_a_reservation_in_a_lane_behind_trunk_commits_through_the_integrity_floor; tests/test_id_carrier_git.py::test_the_claim_folder_reader_reads_each_lanes_work_items_at_a_revision; tests/test_id_carrier_git.py::test_fold_ids_on_a_conflicted_watermark\\\"\\\"\\\"'\nEdit 'docs/test/test-cases.toml' 'test.TC-402' 'evidence' 'evidence = \\\"\\\"\\\"tests/test_id_landing.py::test_the_extracted_sweep_equals_the_working_sweep_for_every_carrier_space; tests/test_id_landing.py::test_a_minus_000_placeholder_is_never_added; tests/test_id_landing.py::test_landing_fold_lag_reads_a_commit_and_an_index_tree; tests/test_id_landing.py::test_a_registry_an_export_ignore_rule_hides_is_still_judged; tests/test_id_landing.py::test_the_slot_refuses_each_unreserved_landing; tests/test_id_landing.py::test_the_slot_refuses_an_unreserved_id_an_export_ignore_rule_hides; tests/test_id_landing.py::test_the_slot_rung_refuses_ids_added_under_an_unreadable_claim; tests/test_id_landing.py::test_the_slot_lands_a_lane_whose_ids_sit_in_its_own_record; tests/test_id_landing.py::test_a_code_only_lane_with_no_carrier_lands; tests/test_id_landing.py::test_the_slot_lands_a_code_only_lane_after_trunk_deletes_an_id_it_based_on; tests/test_id_landing.py::test_the_slot_refuses_a_retired_id_re_authored_inside_its_own_reservation; tests/tes